---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { isStaging } from "../../config";
import { resolveLinuxDownloads } from "../../linuxDownloads";

const { installerUrl, checksumUrl } = await resolveLinuxDownloads(isStaging);
---

<Layout
  title="Install Tearleads on Linux"
  description="Download and install Tearleads on Linux x64."
>
  <main class="website-main">
    <h1>Install Tearleads on Linux</h1>
    <p>
      The Linux download supports x64 processors from Intel and AMD.
      We test it on Ubuntu 24.04.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install the desktop libraries. On Ubuntu 24.04, run:
        <pre><code>sudo apt install libgtk-3-0 libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 libayatana-appindicator3-1 librsvg2-2 libnss3 libasound2t64 libgbm1</code></pre>
      </li>
      <li><a href={installerUrl}>Download the Linux archive</a> and its <a href={checksumUrl}>SHA-256 checksum</a>.</li>
      <li>Verify the download by running <code>sha256sum -c</code> followed by the checksum filename.</li>
      <li>Extract the <code>.tar.gz</code> archive using your file manager.</li>
      <li>Open a terminal in the extracted folder and run <code>./installer</code> as your regular user.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The installer adds Tearleads to your application menu and opens the app.
      A desktop session is required.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  li {
    margin-block: 16px;
  }
  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 16px;
    background: #f3f5f2;
  }
</style>
